        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Add auto sizes fallback img doc]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40906</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40906"/>
        <updated>2025-08-27T13:18:11.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/193881290?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #40902.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3358556428" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40902" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/40902/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40902">#40902</a></h3>
<h3 dir="auto">Summary</h3>
<p dir="auto">Added clarification for the auto keyword and fallback values in the sizes attribute of the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href=""><img style="max-width: 100%;"></a> element. This ensures developers know how to maintain backward compatibility for browsers that do not support auto.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Problem</h3>
<p dir="auto">The existing MDN documentation did not mention:<br>
How to specify fallback values when using auto.<br>
The importance of ordering fallback values for older browsers.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">What Changed</h3>
<p dir="auto">Updated the sizes attribute description.<br>
Added note about backward compatibility.<br>
Included an example from the HTML specification.</p>
